  "id": "residual-schizophrenia",
  "term": "residual schizophrenia",
  "definition": "Residual schizophrenia is a form of schizophrenia in which a person has previously had a schizophrenia episode, but the prominent psychotic symptoms are no longer present. Ongoing features may remain as negative symptoms, such as reduced emotional expression or lack of motivation, or as milder positive symptoms, such as unusual beliefs.",
